1 Overview
**********

Sake is a build system designed to replace classical Makefile-based
tools with declarative GNU Guile Scheme code.  Instead of relying on a
custom, macro-heavy DSL, Sake leverages Scheme procedures to construct a
Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) of build targets and their dependencies.

   Key concepts in Sake:
   • *Target*: A named goal, usually corresponding to an output file or
     a pseudo-target.
   • *Dependencies*: A list of files or other targets that must be up to
     date before the target is processed.
   • *Recipe*: A shell command executed to update the target when any
     dependency is newer than the target file.


