5 Environment Variables and ‘sakevar’
*************************************

In traditional Makefiles, variables automatically inherit values from
shell environment variables with default fallbacks (e.g., ‘CC ?= gcc’).

   To keep syntax concise and avoid verbose calls to ‘or’ and ‘getenv’,
Sake provides the ‘sakevar’ macro.

 -- Macro: sakevar variable default-value
     Binds VARIABLE to the value of its corresponding uppercase shell
     environment variable.  If the environment variable is unset or
     empty, it falls back to DEFAULT-VALUE.

   For example:

     (sakevar cc "gcc")
     (sakevar cflags "-O2 -Wall")
     (sakevar ldflags "-lncursesw")

   This macro automatically inspects the environment for ‘CC’, ‘CFLAGS’,
and ‘LDFLAGS’, expanding at compile time to:

     (define cc (or (getenv "CC") "gcc"))
     (define cflags (or (getenv "CFLAGS") "-O2 -Wall"))
     (define ldflags (or (getenv "LDFLAGS") "-lncursesw"))


