6 Rules and Targets
*******************

6.1 The ‘target’ Procedure
==========================

The primary primitive in Sake is the ‘target’ procedure.  It registers a
node in the internal build graph.

 -- Scheme Procedure: target name [#:deps deps] [#:cmd cmd]
     Registers a build target named NAME.

        • NAME: A string naming the target file or abstract goal (e.g.,
          ‘"all"’).
        • #:DEPS: A list of strings representing file or target
          dependencies.  Defaults to ‘'()’.
        • #:CMD: A string containing the shell command to execute when
          the target is out of date.  Defaults to ‘""’.

6.2 Dependency Evaluation
=========================

Sake evaluates target modification times against its dependencies.  A
target is considered out of date and recompiled if:
  1. The target file does not exist on disk.
  2. Any file listed in #:DEPS has a newer timestamp than the target
     file.
  3. A dependency is a pseudo-target that was executed in the current
     run.


