7 Pattern Rules and Batch Generation
************************************

In GNU Make, pattern rules use implicit match syntax like ‘%.o: %.c’.
In Sake, pattern generation is expressed procedurally using Guile's
‘for-each’ procedure.

     (define sources '("main" "utils" "parser"))

     ;; Generate rules for compiling each .c file into a .o file
     (for-each
       (lambda (name)
         (let ((c-file (format #f "~a.c" name))
               (o-file (format #f "~a.o" name)))
           (target o-file
                   #:deps (list c-file)
                   #:cmd (format #f "~a ~a -c ~a -o ~a" cc cflags c-file o-file))))
       sources)

   This explicit approach eliminates implicit rule resolution bugs while
retaining the concise nature of pattern rules.


