8 Abstract (Phony) Targets
**************************

In GNU Make, targets that do not produce output files require a special
‘.PHONY’ declaration.  In Sake, abstract goals such as ‘"clean"’ or
‘"install"’ require no special syntax.  Because their corresponding
files do not exist on disk, Sake automatically considers them out of
date and executes their recipe command whenever invoked.

     (target "clean"
             #:deps '()
             #:cmd "rm -f *.o my_program")


